\title{Notes}
\author{dhsorens}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    I am interested, broadly speaking, in formal proposition and proof.
    From a high level, what tends to catch my attention is the nuance of going from an intuitive, abstract idea into something formal—whether it's a formal specification of a program, a formalized theorem statement, or even something simply written out as a program.
}

\p{
    During my PhD this manifested as written work focused on the problem of (correctly) specifying and formally verifying [financial smart contracts](dhsorens-000A).
    But I continue to be interested in [software verification more broadly](dhsorens-0015), the ongoing work to [formalize mathematics](dhsorens-000Z), and other developments in using [proof assistants](dhsorens-000B) in production.
}

\p{
    I recently started work on formally verifying [all things zero-knowledge](dhsorens-0020) on the Ethereum protocol, so my interests are broadening but are still rooted in the same topics.
}

% This page is an index, not a container: entries link out rather than
% transclude, so it stays a readable feed however large the forest gets.
% Newest first. Comment an entry out to unlist it.
\p{Newest first:

    \ul{
        \li{[zkVMs and SNARKs](dhsorens-002C). A systematic study of the cryptography and machine architecture these systems are built from, topic by topic: [arithmetisation](dhsorens-002R), [commitment schemes](dhsorens-002Z), [low-degree testing](dhsorens-0036) from FRI to WHIR, [zkVMs](dhsorens-003Q) themselves, and [formalising the stack](dhsorens-003Z) in Lean. August 2026.}
        \li{[LC3 in Lean](dhsorens-0027). A small virtual machine and its semantics in Lean, with the [ISA-level details](dhsorens-0029) and the [proofs of correctness](dhsorens-002A) written up separately. March 2026.}
        \li{[CompPoly and Computable Specifications](dhsorens-0025). Why an executable specification is a stronger specification, and how that connects to [metaspecifications](dhsorens-000L) in cryptography. March 2026.}
        \li{[Protocol Snarkification](dhsorens-0020). Ongoing work to integrate zero knowledge proofs into every layer of the Ethereum protocol. December 2025.}
        \li{[Formal Specification and Verification](dhsorens-000U). [Smart contract specification and verification](dhsorens-000W), and [formal verification in proof assistants](dhsorens-0015) more broadly. August 2025.}
        \li{[Type Theory and Formal Proof](dhsorens-000V). [Proof assistants](dhsorens-000B), some preliminary work in [HoTT](dhsorens-hott), and the [formalization of mathematics](dhsorens-000Z) in [Lean](dhsorens-lean). August 2025.}
        % \li{[How the Formalization of Mathematics Relates to My Work](dhsorens-0017). September 2025.}
    }
}
